{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "next-cursor": "MTc5NDUxMDA0NDAwMCwxMC4xMTI2JTJGc2NpZW5jZS5hZWYzMTUw", "total-results": 226, "items": [{"license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 11, 12]], "date-time": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1794441600000}, "content-version": "stm-asf", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.15223/policy-029"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 11, 12]], "date-time": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1794441600000}, "content-version": "stm-asf", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.15223/policy-037"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 11, 12]], "date-time": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1794441600000}, "content-version": "stm-asf", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.15223/policy-045"}], "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Thiamine diphosphate (ThDP)-dependent enzymes are versatile biocatalysts for carbon–carbon bond formation, yet their catalytic repertoire has been largely confined to linear homologation and intramolecular cyclizations that rely on single-site reactive intermediates such as the Breslow or ketyl radical species. Intermolecular annulation─a powerful strategy for constructing cyclic architectures─has remained elusive within this enzyme class. Here, we report the first intermolecular [3 + 2] annulation catalyzed by a ThDP-dependent enzyme, achieved through a homoenolate-mediated nucleophilic addition pathway. A phylogeny-guided enzyme mining identified a previously uncharacterized enzyme from Variovorax boronicumulans(ThDP-5), and subsequent protein engineering yielded the F484S variant, which exhibits markedly enhanced activity and exquisite stereocontrol. This biocatalytic system exhibits a broad substrate scope (30 examples), accommodating diverse substituted cinnamaldehydes and isatins to afford chiral spirooxindole lactones with excellent stereoselectivity (up to &amp;gt; 20:1 dr and 99% ee). Preparative-scale reactions (2 mmol) validate its synthetic utility. This work expands ThDP-dependent biocatalysis to intermolecular annulations, providing a robust and selective platform for the construction of pharmaceutically relevant spirocyclic architectures.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1021/jacs.6c14033", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 11, 12]], "date-time": "2026-11-12T23:02:01Z", "timestamp": 1794524521000}, "title": ["Reprogramming ThDP-Dependent\nEnzyme for Intermolecular\n[3 + 2] Annulation via a Homoenolate Intermediate"], "author": [{"given": "Huimin", "family": "Liu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "East China University of Science and Technology , , ,", "place": ["Shanghai, China, 200237"]}, {"name": "Chinese Academy of Sciences , , ,", "place": ["Shenzhen, China, 518055"]}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yinhong", "family": "Lai", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "East China University of Science and Technology , , ,", "place": ["Shanghai, China, 200237"]}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Huangong", "family": "Li", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "East China University of Science and Technology , , ,", "place": ["Shanghai, China, 200237"]}, {"name": "Chinese Academy of Sciences , , ,", "place": ["Shenzhen, China, 518055"]}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Xuesi", "family": "Chen", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "East China University of Science and Technology , , ,", "place": ["Shanghai, China, 200237"]}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Lintao", "family": "Pan", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "East China University of Science and Technology , , ,", "place": ["Shanghai, China, 200237"]}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Tiantian", "fami